<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>The feature-matching loss profile and its optimal behavior</h3>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> show the conditional feature-matching loss defined in (<a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 2.1 The feature-matching loss ‣ 2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), plotted against the completion length <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. We refer to the function that maps <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> to the corresponding (conditional) feature-matching loss value as the <em id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(conditional) feature-matching loss profile</em>.
To compute conditional feature-matching loss values, we extract ground-truth pairs <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c,y)</annotation></semantics></math> from long ground-truth token sequences by <em id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">selecting a strided set of prefixes of the sequence as the contexts <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, and the ensuing windows of length <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> as the completions <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math></em>.
The bias-variance decomposition (<a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 2.1 The feature-matching loss ‣ 2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) directly implies that the minimum value of <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{CFM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>CFM</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{CFM}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]</annotation></semantics></math>.
The following lemma shows that <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]</annotation></semantics></math> is non-decreasing with the completion length <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(The optimal conditional feature-matching profile)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the assumptions</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{c}(y):=\phi(c\!:\!y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{c}(y):=\phi(c\!:\!y)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> depends on </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> only through their concatenation </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\!:\!y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">:</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\!:\!y</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, which follows the construction in </span><a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 The feature-matching loss ‣ 2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Context-completion pairs </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c,y)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are selected/sampled from long ground-truth sequences as described above, such that for a fixed completion length </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, concatenations </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c:y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c:y</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are equally distributed to contexts </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Neglecting edge effects that stem from the long ground-truth sequences being finite, this holds for example if contexts are sampled as random prefixes of the ground-truth sequence.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the optimal conditional feature-matching loss profile <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]</annotation></semantics></math> is non-decreasing with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and admits the bound</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]\leq\mathrm{Var}_{c\sim p}[\phi(c)]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]\leq\mathrm{Var}_{c\sim p}[\phi(c)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider completion lengths <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq G^{\prime}\leq G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq G^{\prime}\leq G</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y,\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y,\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math> denote sequences of length <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime},\hat{y}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime},\hat{y}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> completions of length <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime\prime},\hat{y}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime\prime},\hat{y}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> completions of length <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime\prime}=G-G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime\prime}=G-G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, which means that we write the optimal conditional feature-matching loss at completion lengths <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime})|c]\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">:</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime})|c]\big]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi(c\!:\!y)|c]\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi(c\!:\!y)|c]\big]</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Observe that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim p}\Big[\big\|\phi_{c}(y)\big\|^{2}\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big\|^{2}\Big]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\phi(c)\big\|^{2}\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}\big[\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c:y^{\prime\prime})}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime\prime}\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big]\big\|^{2}\Big]\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>Var</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.216em;" width="0.216em"><mo>:</mo></mpadded><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mpadded style="width:0.216em;" width="0.216em"><mo lspace="0.108em">:</mo></mpadded><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim p}\Big[\big\|\phi_{c}(y)\big\|^{2}\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big\|^{2}\Big]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\phi(c)\big\|^{2}\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}\big[\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c:y^{\prime\prime})}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime\prime}\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big]\big\|^{2}\Big]\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here, the second equality holds because <math id="A1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c:y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c:y</annotation></semantics></math> is equally distributed to <math id="A1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> by Assumption <em id="A1.p2.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(b)</em>, and using the tower property of expectation together with the decomposition <math id="A1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=y^{\prime\prime}\!:\!y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.108em">:</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=y^{\prime\prime}\!:\!y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Jensen’s inequality, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}\big[\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c:y^{\prime\prime})}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime\prime}\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big]\big\|^{2}\Big]\leq\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c:y^{\prime\prime})}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime\prime}\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big\|^{2}\Big]\Big]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{(c,y^{\prime\prime})\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c:y^{\prime\prime})}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime\prime}\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big\|^{2}\Big]=\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big\|^{2}\Big]\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.216em;" width="0.216em"><mo>:</mo></mpadded><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mpadded style="width:0.216em;" width="0.216em"><mo lspace="0.108em">:</mo></mpadded><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.216em;" width="0.216em"><mo>:</mo></mpadded><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mpadded style="width:0.216em;" width="0.216em"><mo lspace="0.108em">:</mo></mpadded><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.216em;" width="0.216em"><mo>:</mo></mpadded><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mpadded style="width:0.216em;" width="0.216em"><mo lspace="0.108em">:</mo></mpadded><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.216em;" width="0.216em"><mo>:</mo></mpadded><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}\big[\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c:y^{\prime\prime})}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime\prime}\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big]\big\|^{2}\Big]\leq\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c:y^{\prime\prime})}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime\prime}\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big\|^{2}\Big]\Big]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{(c,y^{\prime\prime})\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c:y^{\prime\prime})}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime\prime}\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big\|^{2}\Big]=\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big\|^{2}\Big]\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging this back into the right-hand side of (<a href="#A1.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix A The feature-matching loss profile and its optimal behavior ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]&amp;\geq\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\phi(c)\big\|^{2}\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big\|^{2}\Big]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim p}\Big[\big\|\phi_{c}(y)\big\|^{2}\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big\|^{2}\Big]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y^{\prime})|c]\big],\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>Var</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.216em;" width="0.216em"><mo>:</mo></mpadded><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.216em;" width="0.216em"><mo>:</mo></mpadded><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>Var</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]&amp;\geq\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\phi(c)\big\|^{2}\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big\|^{2}\Big]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim p}\Big[\big\|\phi_{c}(y)\big\|^{2}\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi(c\!:\!y^{\prime})]\big\|^{2}\Big]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}_{y^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y^{\prime})|c]\big],\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">which concludes the proof that the optimal conditional feature-matching loss is non-decreasing with the completion length <math id="A1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. To prove the bound (<a href="#A1.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ Lemma A.1 (The optimal conditional feature-matching profile). ‣ Appendix A The feature-matching loss profile and its optimal behavior ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>), we apply Jensen’s inequality in the opposite direction:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big\|^{2}\Big]\geq\big\|\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim p}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big\|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big\|^{2}\Big]\geq\big\|\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim p}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">and plugging this into (<a href="#A1.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix A The feature-matching loss profile and its optimal behavior ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]\leq\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim p}\Big[\big\|\phi_{c}(y)\big\|^{2}\Big]-\big\|\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim p}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\mathrm{Var}_{(c,y)\sim p}[\phi(c\!:\!y)]=\mathrm{Var}_{c\sim p}[\phi(c)]\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>Var</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.216em;" width="0.216em"><mo>:</mo></mpadded><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathrm{Var}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)|c]\big]\leq\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim p}\Big[\big\|\phi_{c}(y)\big\|^{2}\Big]-\big\|\mathbb{E}_{(c,y)\sim p}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big\|^{2}\\
&amp;=\mathrm{Var}_{(c,y)\sim p}[\phi(c\!:\!y)]=\mathrm{Var}_{c\sim p}[\phi(c)]\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Feature matching with whitening</h3>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section motivates a <em id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">whitened</em> variant of feature matching by connecting standard cross-entropy training to a local <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> objective. Then, we relax a variational formulation of the <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> divergence by restricting the function space to a generalized linear model space corresponding to a chosen feature map. The resulting optimization problem admits a closed form and corresponds to the feature-matching loss with whitening, which amounts to premultiplying the feature vectors by the inverse of the matrix of second moments. However, in practice we only have access to a low-rank approximation of this matrix, which means that we can only compute a pseudo-inverse. We describe different empirical loss variants that we tried, including the one that we used to obtain the results in the main paper.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Relating cross-entropy training to a <math id="A2.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> divergence objective</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a context <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> and consider completions <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>G</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math> (for some completion length <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>). Let <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot\mid c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot\mid c)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the ground-truth conditional distribution over completions and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)</annotation></semantics></math> the model distribution. Cross-entropy training minimizes the conditional KL divergence</p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}p(y\mid c)\log\frac{p(y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>G</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}p(y\mid c)\log\frac{p(y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Rewriting (<a href="#A2.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ B.1 Relating cross-entropy training to a 𝜒^2 divergence objective ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) as an expectation under <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}p_{\theta}(y\mid c)\,\frac{p(y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}\log\frac{p(y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>G</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}p_{\theta}(y\mid c)\,\frac{p(y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}\log\frac{p(y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The first-order Taylor expansion of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto x\log x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto x\log x</annotation></semantics></math> around <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=1</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x\log x=(x-1)+\tfrac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}+O\big((x-1)^{3}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x\log x=(x-1)+\tfrac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}+O\big((x-1)^{3}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Plugging (<a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ B.1 Relating cross-entropy training to a 𝜒^2 divergence objective ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) into (<a href="#A2.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ B.1 Relating cross-entropy training to a 𝜒^2 divergence objective ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) yields</p>
<table id="A2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big)&amp;=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}p_{\theta}(y\mid c)\Big(\tfrac{p(y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}-1\Big)^{2}+\sum_{y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}p_{\theta}(y\mid c)\,O\!\Big(\Big(\tfrac{p(y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}-1\Big)^{3}\Big)\\
&amp;=\tfrac{1}{2}\,D_{\chi^{2}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big)+\sum_{y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}p_{\theta}(y\mid c)\,O\!\Big(\Big(\tfrac{p(y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}-1\Big)^{3}\Big),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.686em;" width="0.686em"><mi>D</mi></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.062em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.507em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>G</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>G</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.451em;" width="0.451em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.686em;" width="0.686em"><mi>D</mi></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.062em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.507em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>G</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.340em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.451em;" width="0.451em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big)&amp;=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}p_{\theta}(y\mid c)\Big(\tfrac{p(y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}-1\Big)^{2}+\sum_{y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}p_{\theta}(y\mid c)\,O\!\Big(\Big(\tfrac{p(y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}-1\Big)^{3}\Big)\\
&amp;=\tfrac{1}{2}\,D_{\chi^{2}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big)+\sum_{y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}p_{\theta}(y\mid c)\,O\!\Big(\Big(\tfrac{p(y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}-1\Big)^{3}\Big),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> divergence is</p>
<table id="A2.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\chi^{2}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big):=\sum_{y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}\frac{\big(p(y\mid c)-p_{\theta}(y\mid c)\big)^{2}}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}=\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)}\!\Big[\Big(\tfrac{p(Y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(Y\mid c)}-1\Big)^{2}\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>G</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\chi^{2}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big):=\sum_{y\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}\frac{\big(p(y\mid c)-p_{\theta}(y\mid c)\big)^{2}}{p_{\theta}(y\mid c)}=\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)}\!\Big[\Big(\tfrac{p(Y\mid c)}{p_{\theta}(Y\mid c)}-1\Big)^{2}\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot\mid c)\approx p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot\mid c)\approx p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)</annotation></semantics></math> (so the ratio <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p/p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p/p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is close to <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>), the remainder term in (<a href="#A2.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ B.1 Relating cross-entropy training to a 𝜒^2 divergence objective ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) can be neglected, and we obtain the local approximation</p>
<table id="A2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big)\approx\tfrac{1}{2}\,D_{\chi^{2}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big)\approx\tfrac{1}{2}\,D_{\chi^{2}}\!\big(p(\cdot\mid c)\,\|\,p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid c)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Relaxing a variational formulation of the <math id="A2.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> divergence to a linear feature class</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The representation (<a href="#A2.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ B.1 Relating cross-entropy training to a 𝜒^2 divergence objective ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) makes explicit that <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\chi^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\chi^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to an <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> discrepancy in the space of one-hot features. Next, we want to express the <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> divergence, or rather a relaxation of it, in terms of generic feature maps. For that, we consider a variational representation of the <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> divergence.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Variational representation of the chi-squared divergence)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> be probability measures on a measurable space <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\ll Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\ll Q</annotation></semantics></math>, and write their Radon–Nikodym derivative as <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(y)=\frac{dP}{dQ}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(y)=\frac{dP}{dQ}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\chi^{2}}(P\|Q)=\sup_{f\in L^{2}(Q),\,\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}[f(Y)]=0}\Big\{\,2\,(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim P}[f(Y)]-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}[f(Y)])-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}[f(Y)^{2}]\,\Big\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\chi^{2}}(P\|Q)=\sup_{f\in L^{2}(Q),\,\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}[f(Y)]=0}\Big\{\,2\,(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim P}[f(Y)]-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}[f(Y)])-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}[f(Y)^{2}]\,\Big\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, the supremum is attained at <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\star}(y)=r(y)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\star}(y)=r(y)-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(y)=\frac{dP}{dQ}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(y)=\frac{dP}{dQ}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{Q}[r(Y)]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{Q}[r(Y)]=1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\chi^{2}(P\|Q)=\mathbb{E}_{Q}\big[(g(Y)-1)^{2}\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}(P\|Q)=\mathbb{E}_{Q}\big[(g(Y)-1)^{2}\big]</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L^{2}(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L^{2}(Q)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\,(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f(Y)]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)])-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\,(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f(Y)]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)])-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\,\mathbb{E}_{Q}[(g(Y)-1)f(Y)]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)^{2}]=\mathbb{E}_{Q}\!\big[2(g(Y)-1)f(Y)-f(Y)^{2}\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\,\mathbb{E}_{Q}[(g(Y)-1)f(Y)]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)^{2}]=\mathbb{E}_{Q}\!\big[2(g(Y)-1)f(Y)-f(Y)^{2}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Completing the square pointwise gives
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2(g-1)f-f^{2}=-(f-g+1)^{2}+(r-1)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2(g-1)f-f^{2}=-(f-g+1)^{2}+(r-1)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\,(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f(Y)]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)])-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)^{2}]=\mathbb{E}_{Q}[(g(Y)-1)^{2}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[(f(Y)-g(Y)+1)^{2}]\leq\mathbb{E}_{Q}[(g(Y)-1)^{2}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\,(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f(Y)]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)])-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)^{2}]=\mathbb{E}_{Q}[(g(Y)-1)^{2}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[(f(Y)-g(Y)+1)^{2}]\leq\mathbb{E}_{Q}[(g(Y)-1)^{2}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">with equality iff
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=g-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=g-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{f\in L^{2}(Q)}\Big\{2\,(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f(Y)]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)])-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)^{2}]\Big\}=\mathbb{E}_{Q}[(g(Y)-1)^{2}]=D_{\chi^{2}}(P\|Q)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{f\in L^{2}(Q)}\Big\{2\,(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f(Y)]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)])-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f(Y)^{2}]\Big\}=\mathbb{E}_{Q}[(g(Y)-1)^{2}]=D_{\chi^{2}}(P\|Q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the optimum is achieved at <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=g(x)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=g(x)-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We particularize Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Variational representation of the chi-squared divergence). ‣ B.2 Relaxing a variational formulation of the 𝜒^2 divergence to a linear feature class ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> in the language model setting.
Let <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi:\mathcal{V}^{G}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>G</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi:\mathcal{V}^{G}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a feature map over completions (in our setting, the natural choice is <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(y)=\phi_{c}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(y)=\phi_{c}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>, the feature-network embedding of the concatenated sequence). Restricting the supremum in (<a href="#A2.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Lemma B.1 (Variational representation of the chi-squared divergence). ‣ B.2 Relaxing a variational formulation of the 𝜒^2 divergence to a linear feature class ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) to generalized linear model <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{w}(y)=w^{\top}\varphi(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{w}(y)=w^{\top}\varphi(y)</annotation></semantics></math> yields the relaxation</p>
<table id="A2.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\chi^{2}}(P\|Q)\geq\sup_{w\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\Big\{\,2\,\big(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim P}\big[w^{\top}\varphi(Y)\big]-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}\big[w^{\top}\varphi(Y)\big]\big)-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}\big[(w^{\top}\varphi(Y))^{2}\big]\,\Big\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn> 2</mn><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\chi^{2}}(P\|Q)\geq\sup_{w\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\Big\{\,2\,\big(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim P}\big[w^{\top}\varphi(Y)\big]-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}\big[w^{\top}\varphi(Y)\big]\big)-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}\big[(w^{\top}\varphi(Y))^{2}\big]\,\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We can rewrite the expression in the supremum as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\,\big(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim P}\big[w^{\top}\varphi(Y)\big]-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}\big[w^{\top}\varphi(Y)\big]\big)-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}\big[\big(w^{\top}\varphi(Y)\big)^{2}\big]=2w^{\top}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})-w^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}w," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\,\big(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim P}\big[w^{\top}\varphi(Y)\big]-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}\big[w^{\top}\varphi(Y)\big]\big)-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}\big[\big(w^{\top}\varphi(Y)\big)^{2}\big]=2w^{\top}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})-w^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}w,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{P}=\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim P}[\varphi(Y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{P}=\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim P}[\varphi(Y)]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{Q}=\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}[\varphi(Y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{Q}=\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}[\varphi(Y)]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{Q}=\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}\big[\varphi(Y)\varphi(Y)^{\top}\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{Q}=\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim Q}\big[\varphi(Y)\varphi(Y)^{\top}\big]</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible, the supremum in (<a href="#A2.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ B.2 Relaxing a variational formulation of the 𝜒^2 divergence to a linear feature class ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) is attained at</p>
<table id="A2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{w}=\Sigma_{Q}^{-1}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{w}=\Sigma_{Q}^{-1}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">and the optimal value is</p>
<table id="A2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{w}\{2w^{\top}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})-w^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}w\}=(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})\,\Sigma_{Q}^{-1}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>w</mi></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{w}\{2w^{\top}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})-w^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}w\}=(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})\,\Sigma_{Q}^{-1}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Thus, assuming that <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Sigma_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}=\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}=\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible, we define the whitened feature matching loss as</p>
<table id="A2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{WFM}}(\theta)\!&amp;=\!\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big)^{\top}\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\quad\times\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]^{-1}\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big)\big],\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>WFM</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.716em;" width="0.716em"><mo>=</mo></mpadded><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.160em;" width="0.160em"><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.160em;" width="0.160em"><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{WFM}}(\theta)\!&amp;=\!\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big)^{\top}\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\quad\times\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]^{-1}\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big)\big],\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Observe that the dependence of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{WFM}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>WFM</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{WFM}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is through <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]</annotation></semantics></math> as in <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{FM}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>FM</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{FM}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, but also through <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. While applying the REINFORCE argument to estimate the gradient for the former can be done as in <a href="#S2" title="2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the approach breaks down for the latter. We decide to disregard the gradient with respect to <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which amounts to the following loss:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{WFM}}(\theta)\!&amp;=\!\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big)^{\top}\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\quad\times\mathrm{stopgrad}\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]\big)^{-1}\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big)\big],\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>WFM</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.716em;" width="0.716em"><mo>=</mo></mpadded><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.160em;" width="0.160em"><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.160em;" width="0.160em"><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{WFM}}(\theta)\!&amp;=\!\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big)^{\top}\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\quad\times\mathrm{stopgrad}\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]\big)^{-1}\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big)\big],\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Dealing with non-invertible second moment matrices <math id="A2.SS3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Sigma_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}</annotation></semantics></math>: a first approach</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The matrix <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Sigma_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}=\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}=\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]</annotation></semantics></math> and especially its empirical version <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\Sigma}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}=\frac{1}{n}\!\sum_{j=1}^{n}\!\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Sigma}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}=\frac{1}{n}\!\sum_{j=1}^{n}\!\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> are often not invertible, in particular when the feature dimension <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is high and/or the number of samples per prompt <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is low. In particular, the rank of the empirical matrix is upper-bounded by the number of samples per prompt, meaning that it is never invertible when <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&lt;d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&lt;d</annotation></semantics></math>, which is usually the case. Thus, we need to solve <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{w}\{2w^{\top}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})-w^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}w\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{w}\{2w^{\top}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})-w^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}w\}</annotation></semantics></math> for general positive semidefinite <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>. More generally, consider maximizing a functional of the form <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(w)=2\langle w,b\rangle-\langle w,\Sigma w\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(w)=2\langle w,b\rangle-\langle w,\Sigma w\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> be an eigendecomposition, and write <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=\sum_{i}\alpha_{i}u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=\sum_{i}\alpha_{i}u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\sum_{i}\beta_{i}u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\sum_{i}\beta_{i}u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A2.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(w)=2\sum_{i}\alpha_{i}\beta_{i}-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\alpha_{i}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(w)=2\sum_{i}\alpha_{i}\beta_{i}-\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\alpha_{i}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Splitting into nonzero and zero eigenvalues yields the dichotomy:</p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> has any component in <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ker(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ker(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., there exists <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>), then <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{w}f(w)=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{w}f(w)=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and there is no maximizer in <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\perp\ker(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\perp\ker(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\mathrm{Im}(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\mathrm{Im}(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>, then the supremum is finite and equals</p>
<table id="A2.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{w}f(w)=\sum_{\lambda_{i}&gt;0}\frac{\beta_{i}^{2}}{\lambda_{i}}=b^{\top}\,\Sigma^{\dagger}b," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>w</mi></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{w}f(w)=\sum_{\lambda_{i}&gt;0}\frac{\beta_{i}^{2}}{\lambda_{i}}=b^{\top}\,\Sigma^{\dagger}b,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\dagger}=\sum_{\lambda_{i}&gt;0}\frac{1}{\lambda_{i}}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\dagger}=\sum_{\lambda_{i}&gt;0}\frac{1}{\lambda_{i}}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Moore–Penrose pseudoinverse.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In our case, <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\Sigma_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\Sigma_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>. While <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{Q}\perp\ker(\Sigma_{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>⟂</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{Q}\perp\ker(\Sigma_{Q})</annotation></semantics></math> by construction, in general <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> will have non-zero components in <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ker(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ker(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>, and in that case <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{w}\{2w^{\top}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})-w^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}w\}=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{w}\{2w^{\top}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})-w^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}w\}=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. This is not surprising given that when the inequality (<a href="#A2.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ B.2 Relaxing a variational formulation of the 𝜒^2 divergence to a linear feature class ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) holds with equality, which is the case for one-hot feature maps, <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sup_{w}\{2w^{\top}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})-w^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}w\}=\chi^{2}(P\|Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{w}\{2w^{\top}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})-w^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}w\}=\chi^{2}(P\|Q)</annotation></semantics></math>, and it is easy to see that <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\chi^{2}(P\|Q)=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}(P\|Q)=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> when the support of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is larger than the support of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>. To obtain a finite value, it is convenient to replace <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> by the projection <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pr}_{\mathrm{Im}(\Sigma_{Q})}\mu_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pr}_{\mathrm{Im}(\Sigma_{Q})}\mu_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by equation (<a href="#A2.E35" title="Equation 35 ‣ Item (ii) ‣ B.3 Dealing with non-invertible second moment matrices Σ_{𝑝_𝜃(⋅|𝑐)}: a first approach ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{w}\{2w^{\top}(\mathrm{Pr}_{\mathrm{Im}(\Sigma_{Q})}\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})-w^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}w\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>w</mi></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{w}\{2w^{\top}(\mathrm{Pr}_{\mathrm{Im}(\Sigma_{Q})}\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})-w^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}w\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\mathrm{Pr}_{\mathrm{Im}(\Sigma_{Q})}\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}^{\dagger}(\mathrm{Pr}_{\mathrm{Im}(\Sigma_{Q})}\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\mathrm{Pr}_{\mathrm{Im}(\Sigma_{Q})}\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}^{\dagger}(\mathrm{Pr}_{\mathrm{Im}(\Sigma_{Q})}\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}^{\dagger}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q})^{\top}\Sigma_{Q}^{\dagger}(\mu_{P}-\mu_{Q}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where the last equality holds because <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ker(\Sigma_{Q}^{\dagger})=\ker(\Sigma_{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ker(\Sigma_{Q}^{\dagger})=\ker(\Sigma_{Q})</annotation></semantics></math>, and that <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{P}=\mathrm{Pr}_{\mathrm{Im}(\Sigma)}\mu_{P}+\mathrm{Pr}_{\ker(\Sigma)}\mu_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{P}=\mathrm{Pr}_{\mathrm{Im}(\Sigma)}\mu_{P}+\mathrm{Pr}_{\ker(\Sigma)}\mu_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the following loss function is numerically robust:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{WFM}}(\theta)\!&amp;=\!\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big)^{\top}\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\quad\times\mathrm{stopgrad}\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]\big)^{\dagger}\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big)\big],\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>WFM</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.716em;" width="0.716em"><mo>=</mo></mpadded><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.160em;" width="0.160em"><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.160em;" width="0.160em"><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{WFM}}(\theta)\!&amp;=\!\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big)^{\top}\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\quad\times\mathrm{stopgrad}\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]\big)^{\dagger}\big(\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big)\big],\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">It is easy to compute the gradient of this loss through the framework of <a href="#S2" title="2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>; in the computation of the population reward <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\hat{y},c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\hat{y},c)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Gradient estimation via REINFORCE. ‣ 2.2 Feature-matching rewards and on-policy training ‣ 2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) we simply replace the features <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{c}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{c}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> by the whitened features:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\phi}_{c}(y)=(\Sigma^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(y),\qquad\Sigma_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}=\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\phi}_{c}(y)=(\Sigma^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(y),\qquad\Sigma_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}=\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">and in practice, we compute the reward <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Gradient estimation via REINFORCE. ‣ 2.2 Feature-matching rewards and on-policy training ‣ 2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) using <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m29" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\Sigma}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Sigma}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m30" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Sigma_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\phi}_{c}(y)=(\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(y),\qquad\hat{\Sigma}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\phi}_{c}(y)=(\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(y),\qquad\hat{\Sigma}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Above, <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma^{\dagger})^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma^{\dagger})^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the square root of the pseudo-inverse of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. if <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> admits the eigenvalue decomposition <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\lambda_{i}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m35" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\Sigma^{\dagger})^{1/2}=\sum_{i=1,\lambda_{i}&gt;0}^{d}\lambda_{i}^{-1/2}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma^{\dagger})^{1/2}=\sum_{i=1,\lambda_{i}&gt;0}^{d}\lambda_{i}^{-1/2}u_{i}u_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice, using a function to compute the singular value decomposition of is more numerically stable that using a function to compute the eigenvalue decomposition.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let us write the reward <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> explicitly under whitening:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{j}=\underbrace{2\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\phi_{c}(y)}_{\text{alignment term $\mathrm{AT}_{j}$}}-\underbrace{\frac{2}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})}_{\text{diversity term $\mathrm{DT}_{j}$}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>alignment term </mtext><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">AT</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>diversity term </mtext><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">DT</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{j}=\underbrace{2\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\phi_{c}(y)}_{\text{alignment term $\mathrm{AT}_{j}$}}-\underbrace{\frac{2}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})}_{\text{diversity term $\mathrm{DT}_{j}$}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Suppose that the features <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\big)_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\big)_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of the generated completions are ordered such that repeated completions are arranged consecutively, and that there are exactly <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> different feature vectors among <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\big)_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\big)_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, with multiplicities <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n_{k})_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n_{k})_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{K}n_{k}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{K}n_{k}=n</annotation></semantics></math>. In this section, we make the following assumptions, which hold in practice:</p>
<ol id="A2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The feature dimension <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is larger or equal than the number of generated completions <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. This holds in our experiments, because <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is on the order of thousands, while we take <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=4</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> different feature vectors within <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j}))_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j}))_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are linearly independent. This happens with very high probability in our experiments, also as a consequence of <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\gg n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≫</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\gg n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq k\leq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq k\leq K</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{k}=\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{k-1}n_{k^{\prime}}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{k}=\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{k-1}n_{k^{\prime}}+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the list of feature vectors <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> contains each instance in <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\big)_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\big)_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with multiplicity one. We define the matrices</p>
<ul id="A2.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> as the matrix whose columns are <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j}))_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j}))_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\cdot j}=\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\cdot j}=\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Phi}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Phi}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times K}</annotation></semantics></math> as the matrix whose columns are <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Phi}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Phi}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times K}</annotation></semantics></math> as the matrix whose columns are <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\sqrt{n_{k}}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\sqrt{n_{k}}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Phi}=((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\Phi\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Phi}=((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\Phi\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">And the vectors</p>
<ul id="A2.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi=\phi_{c}(y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi=\phi_{c}(y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\psi}=((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\psi\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\psi}=((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\psi\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(\psi)}=\hat{\Phi}^{\dagger}\psi\in\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(\psi)}=\hat{\Phi}^{\dagger}\psi\in\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is the vector of coefficients of the orthogonal projection of <math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{span}\big(\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}\big)^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{span}\big(\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}\big)^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the basis <math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">We can reexpress the alignment and diversity terms in (<a href="#A2.E41" title="Equation 41 ‣ B.4 Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) with respect to <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{AT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{AT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2n\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}(\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger}\phi_{c}(y)=2n\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}^{\top}\tilde{\psi}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2n\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}(\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger}\phi_{c}(y)=2n\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}^{\top}\tilde{\psi},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{DT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>DT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{DT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2n}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}(\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})=\frac{2n}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\tilde{\Phi}^{\top}_{\cdot j}\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2n}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}(\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})=\frac{2n}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\tilde{\Phi}^{\top}_{\cdot j}\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">The following lemma, proven in <a href="#A2.SS4.SSS1" title="B.4.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ B.4 Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4.1</span></a>, characterizes the inner products <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Phi}^{\top}_{\cdot j}\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Phi}^{\top}_{\cdot j}\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}^{\top}\tilde{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}^{\top}\tilde{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the norm of <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Recall that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{k_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{k_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the multiplicity of the completion <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> within <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\big)_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\big)_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. The inner products between the columns <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j})_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j})_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are given by</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}^{\top}\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}^{\top}\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1/n_{k_{j}}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1/n_{k_{j}}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E44.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{for all }j^{\prime}\text{ such that }\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})=\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})\text{ (in particular }\|\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}\|=1/\sqrt{n_{k_{j}}}\text{)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> such that </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> (in particular </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">)</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{for all }j^{\prime}\text{ such that }\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})=\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})\text{ (in particular }\|\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}\|=1/\sqrt{n_{k_{j}}}\text{)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}^{\top}\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}^{\top}\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E45.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{for all }j^{\prime}\text{ such that }\hat{y}_{j}\neq\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> such that </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{for all }j^{\prime}\text{ such that }\hat{y}_{j}\neq\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">And we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}^{\top}\tilde{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}^{\top}\tilde{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{x^{(\psi)}_{j}}{n_{k_{j}}},\qquad\text{for all $1\leq j\leq n$, and},\qquad\|\tilde{\psi}\|^{2}=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{(x^{(\psi)}_{k})^{2}}{n_{k}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">, and</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{x^{(\psi)}_{j}}{n_{k_{j}}},\qquad\text{for all $1\leq j\leq n$, and},\qquad\|\tilde{\psi}\|^{2}=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{(x^{(\psi)}_{k})^{2}}{n_{k}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, under the conditions of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2. ‣ B.4 Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{AT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{AT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2nx^{(\psi)}_{j}}{n_{k_{j}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2nx^{(\psi)}_{j}}{n_{k_{j}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{DT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>DT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{DT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E48.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2n}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\mathbf{1}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})=\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})]\frac{1}{n_{k_{j}}}=\frac{2n(n_{k_{j}}-1)}{(n-1)n_{k_{j}}}=\frac{2(1-1/n_{k_{j}})}{1-1/n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2n}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\mathbf{1}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})=\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})]\frac{1}{n_{k_{j}}}=\frac{2n(n_{k_{j}}-1)}{(n-1)n_{k_{j}}}=\frac{2(1-1/n_{k_{j}})}{1-1/n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(\psi)}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(\psi)}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th component of <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(\psi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(\psi)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Observe that when <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{c}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{c}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq k\leq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq k\leq K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(\psi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(\psi)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th vector of the canonical basis of <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, which means that <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AT}_{j}=\frac{2n}{n_{k_{j}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AT}_{j}=\frac{2n}{n_{k_{j}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{c}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{c}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, and zero otherwise.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{c}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{c}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is different from all the vectors in <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, the norm of the projection of <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{c}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{c}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{span}\big(\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{span}\big(\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> is usually significantly smaller than the norm of <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{c}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{c}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>, because this subspace is smaller than the ambient dimension as <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\leq n\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\leq n\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>, and this is accentuated the smaller <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is. Observe that in optimizing the empirical rewards <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{j}=\mathrm{AT}_{j}-\mathrm{DT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>DT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{j}=\mathrm{AT}_{j}-\mathrm{DT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, the model balances increasing the alignment term <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and decreasing the diversity term <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>DT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the specific trade-off is determined by the relative sizes of both terms.
Since for small <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> the alignment terms <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathrm{AT}_{j})_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathrm{AT}_{j})_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are small because <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(\psi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(\psi)}</annotation></semantics></math> is abnormally small,
the model focuses on decreasing <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>DT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> as opposed to strongly improving <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Experimentally, this translates to moderate improvements in downstream performance. To achieve more solid boosts in downstream performance, we tested the following alternative approaches:</p>
<ul id="A2.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Variant (i)</span>: <span id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Normalizing the whitened features of the generations and the ground truth in the alignment term</span>. As a result, even when <math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(\psi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(\psi)}</annotation></semantics></math> is small, the alignment term is not. Namely, we set the diversity term <math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>DT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> as in (<a href="#A2.E48" title="Equation 48 ‣ B.4 Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>), and the alignment term <math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{AT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{AT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\phi_{c}(y)}{\big\|(\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\big\|\big\|(\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(y)\big\|}=\frac{2\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}^{\top}\tilde{\psi}}{\big\|\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}\big\|\big\|\tilde{\psi}\big\|}=\frac{2x^{(\psi)}_{j}}{\sqrt{n_{k_{j}}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{(x^{(\psi)}_{k})^{2}}{n_{k}}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">∥</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\phi_{c}(y)}{\big\|(\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\big\|\big\|(\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(y)\big\|}=\frac{2\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}^{\top}\tilde{\psi}}{\big\|\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}\big\|\big\|\tilde{\psi}\big\|}=\frac{2x^{(\psi)}_{j}}{\sqrt{n_{k_{j}}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{(x^{(\psi)}_{k})^{2}}{n_{k}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I5.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Observe that we can write the vector of alignment terms <math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathrm{AT}_{j})_{j=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathrm{AT}_{j})_{j=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A2.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\mathrm{AT}_{j})_{j=1}^{n}=\frac{2(x^{(\psi)}_{j}/\sqrt{n_{j_{k}}})_{j=1}^{n}}{\|(x^{(\psi)}_{j}/\sqrt{n_{j_{k}}})_{j=1}^{n}\|}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\mathrm{AT}_{j})_{j=1}^{n}=\frac{2(x^{(\psi)}_{j}/\sqrt{n_{j_{k}}})_{j=1}^{n}}{\|(x^{(\psi)}_{j}/\sqrt{n_{j_{k}}})_{j=1}^{n}\|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Variant (ii)</span>: <span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Normalizing the whitened features of the generations and the ground truth in the alignment and diversity terms</span>.
We set <math id="A2.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> as in (<a href="#A2.E49" title="Equation 49 ‣ 1st item ‣ B.4 Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>), and <math id="A2.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>DT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathrm{DT}_{j}&amp;=\frac{2}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\frac{\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})}{\big\|(\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\big\|\big\|(\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})\big\|}=\frac{2}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\frac{\tilde{\Phi}^{\top}_{\cdot j}\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}}{\big\|\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}\big\|\big\|\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}\big\|}\\
&amp;=\frac{2}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\mathbf{1}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})=\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})]\frac{\sqrt{n_{k_{j}}n_{k_{j^{\prime}}}}}{n_{k_{j}}}=\frac{2(n_{k_{j}}-1)}{n-1}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>DT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">∥</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub></mrow></msqrt><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathrm{DT}_{j}&amp;=\frac{2}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\frac{\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})}{\big\|(\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})\big\|\big\|(\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})\big\|}=\frac{2}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\frac{\tilde{\Phi}^{\top}_{\cdot j}\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}}{\big\|\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}\big\|\big\|\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}\big\|}\\
&amp;=\frac{2}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\mathbf{1}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})=\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})]\frac{\sqrt{n_{k_{j}}n_{k_{j^{\prime}}}}}{n_{k_{j}}}=\frac{2(n_{k_{j}}-1)}{n-1}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Variant (iii)</span>: <span id="A2.I5.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Normalizing the whitened features of the ground truth in the alignment term</span>. We set <math id="A2.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>DT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> as in (<a href="#A2.E48" title="Equation 48 ‣ B.4 Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>) and <math id="A2.I5.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{AT}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{AT}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\phi_{c}(y)}{\big\|(\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(y)\big\|}=\frac{2\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}^{\top}\tilde{\psi}}{\big\|\tilde{\psi}\big\|}=\frac{2x^{(\psi)}_{j}}{n_{k_{j}}\cdot\frac{1}{\sqrt{n_{k_{j}}}}\cdot\sqrt{\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{(x^{(\psi)}_{k})^{2}}{n_{k}}}}=\frac{2x^{(\psi)}_{j}}{n_{k_{j}}\sqrt{\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{(x^{(\psi)}_{k})^{2}}{n_{k}}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">∥</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\phi_{c}(y)}{\big\|(\hat{\Sigma}^{\dagger}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)})^{1/2}\phi_{c}(y)\big\|}=\frac{2\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}^{\top}\tilde{\psi}}{\big\|\tilde{\psi}\big\|}=\frac{2x^{(\psi)}_{j}}{n_{k_{j}}\cdot\frac{1}{\sqrt{n_{k_{j}}}}\cdot\sqrt{\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{(x^{(\psi)}_{k})^{2}}{n_{k}}}}=\frac{2x^{(\psi)}_{j}}{n_{k_{j}}\sqrt{\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{(x^{(\psi)}_{k})^{2}}{n_{k}}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Experimentally, <span id="A2.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">variant (i) offers the best performance, and is the one that we use in all the whitening experiments we report in this paper.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Observe that when we use whitening (with or without any of these variants), we are not explicitly minimizing a particular loss function on <math id="A2.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, as our REINFORCE-style reward does not take into account that the second-moment matrix <math id="A2.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\Phi}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Phi}_{p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}</annotation></semantics></math> and the normalization factors depend on <math id="A2.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. In the figures of <a href="#A8" title="Appendix H Additional Experimental Results ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span></a>, apart from the non-whitened feature matching loss, we report the proxy quantity:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\big(\mathrm{AT}_{j}-\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{DT}_{j}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>AT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>DT</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\big(\mathrm{AT}_{j}-\frac{1}{2}\mathrm{DT}_{j}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">We refer to this quantity as the ”feature-matching loss with whitening”. Ignoring the dependence of the second-moment matrix and the normalization constants on <math id="A2.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, we view whitened feature matching as trying to decrease this loss.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.4.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2. ‣ B.4 Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a></h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">And we define the matrix <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> as the matrix whose <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th row has value <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\sqrt{n_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\sqrt{n_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> on all positions from <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{k}=\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{k-1}n_{k^{\prime}}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{k}=\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{k-1}n_{k^{\prime}}+1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{k+1}-1=\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{k}n_{k^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{k+1}-1=\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{k}n_{k^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> (both included), and value zero on all remaining positions.
Observe that the rows of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> constitute an orthonormal set, i.e. <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BB^{\top}=\mathrm{Id}\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Id</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BB^{\top}=\mathrm{Id}\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times K}</annotation></semantics></math>, and that by construction,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Phi=\bar{\Phi}B." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Phi=\bar{\Phi}B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\Phi}=((\bar{\Phi}BB^{\top}\bar{\Phi}^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\bar{\Phi}B=((\bar{\Phi}\bar{\Phi}^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\bar{\Phi}B." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\Phi}=((\bar{\Phi}BB^{\top}\bar{\Phi}^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\bar{\Phi}B=((\bar{\Phi}\bar{\Phi}^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\bar{\Phi}B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Next, we inspect <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((\bar{\Phi}\bar{\Phi}^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\bar{\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((\bar{\Phi}\bar{\Phi}^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\bar{\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe that by assumptions <em id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(i)</em> and <em id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.3.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(ii)</em> above, the rank of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Phi}=U\Sigma V^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Phi}=U\Sigma V^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> be the thin singular value decomposition of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times K}</annotation></semantics></math> has orthonormal columns, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times K}</annotation></semantics></math> is an orthogonal matrix, and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times K}</annotation></semantics></math> is a diagonal matrix with strictly positive numbers on the diagonal (in general the singular values are non-negative, but since <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> has rank <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, all of them must be positive). Then, by the definitions of the square root and the pseudo-inverse</p>
<table id="A2.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle((\bar{\Phi}\bar{\Phi}^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\bar{\Phi}=((U\Sigma^{2}U^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}U\Sigma V^{\top}=U\Sigma^{-1}U^{\top}U\Sigma V^{\top}=UV^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle((\bar{\Phi}\bar{\Phi}^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\bar{\Phi}=((U\Sigma^{2}U^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}U\Sigma V^{\top}=U\Sigma^{-1}U^{\top}U\Sigma V^{\top}=UV^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Plugging this into the right-hand side of (<a href="#A2.E55" title="Equation 55 ‣ B.4.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ B.4 Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a>) yields</p>
<table id="A2.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\Phi}=UV^{\top}B." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\Phi}=UV^{\top}B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">And</p>
<table id="A2.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\Phi}^{\top}\tilde{\Phi}=B^{\top}VU^{\top}UV^{\top}B=B^{\top}B," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\Phi}^{\top}\tilde{\Phi}=B^{\top}VU^{\top}UV^{\top}B=B^{\top}B,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which means that for <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j,j^{\prime}\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j,j^{\prime}\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}^{\top}\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j}^{\top}\tilde{\Phi}_{\cdot j^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,j^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,j^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>-th component of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Phi}^{\top}\tilde{\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Phi}^{\top}\tilde{\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, is equal to the <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,j^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,j^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>-th component of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\top}B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\top}B</annotation></semantics></math>, which is <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\cdot j}^{\top}B_{\cdot j^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\cdot j}^{\top}B_{\cdot j^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\cdot j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\cdot j}</annotation></semantics></math>, (resp. <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\cdot j^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\cdot j^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>) has a single non-zero entry <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\sqrt{n_{k_{j}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\sqrt{n_{k_{j}}}</annotation></semantics></math> in position <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\sqrt{n_{k_{j^{\prime}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\sqrt{n_{k_{j^{\prime}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> in position <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{j^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{j^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>), equalities (<a href="#A2.E44" title="Equation 44 ‣ Lemma B.2. ‣ B.4 Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E45" title="Equation 45 ‣ Lemma B.2. ‣ B.4 Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) follow.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let us define the diagonal matrix <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times K}</annotation></semantics></math> with diagonal values <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(1/\sqrt{n_{k}}\big)_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(1/\sqrt{n_{k}}\big)_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that we can express the matrix <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> with columns <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Phi}\bar{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Phi}\bar{B}</annotation></semantics></math>. By construction of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(\psi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(\psi)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi=\hat{\Phi}x^{(\psi)}+\psi^{\prime}=\bar{\Phi}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}+\psi^{\prime}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi=\hat{\Phi}x^{(\psi)}+\psi^{\prime}=\bar{\Phi}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}+\psi^{\prime},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the orthogonal projection of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{span}\big(\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}\big)^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{span}\big(\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}\big)^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, using equation (<a href="#A2.E56" title="Equation 56 ‣ B.4.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ B.4 Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>), and the fact that <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{span}((U_{\cdot k})_{k=1}^{K})=\mathrm{span}\big(\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{span}((U_{\cdot k})_{k=1}^{K})=\mathrm{span}\big(\big(\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j_{k}})\big)_{k=1}^{K}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\psi=((\bar{\Phi}\bar{\Phi}^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\big(\bar{\Phi}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}+\psi^{\prime}\big)=UV^{\top}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}+U\Sigma^{-1}U^{\top}\psi^{\prime}=UV^{\top}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\psi=((\bar{\Phi}\bar{\Phi}^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\big(\bar{\Phi}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}+\psi^{\prime}\big)=UV^{\top}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}+U\Sigma^{-1}U^{\top}\psi^{\prime}=UV^{\top}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Hence, using (<a href="#A2.E57" title="Equation 57 ‣ B.4.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ B.4 Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">57</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E60" title="Equation 60 ‣ B.4.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ B.4 Variants of the whitened feature-matching loss with better empirical performance ‣ Appendix B Feature matching with whitening ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>) yields</p>
<table id="A2.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Phi^{\top}((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\psi=BVU^{\top}UV^{\top}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}=B^{\top}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}=\tilde{B}x^{(\psi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Phi^{\top}((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\psi=BVU^{\top}UV^{\top}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}=B^{\top}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}=\tilde{B}x^{(\psi)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where we define <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> as the matrix whose <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th row has value <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/n_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/n_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> on all positions from <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{k}=\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{k-1}n_{k^{\prime}}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{k}=\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{k-1}n_{k^{\prime}}+1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{k+1}-1=\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{k}n_{k^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{k+1}-1=\sum_{k^{\prime}=1}^{k}n_{k^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> (both included), and value zero on all remaining positions.
And</p>
<table id="A2.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi^{\top}((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\psi=(x^{(\psi)})^{\top}\bar{B}^{\top}VU^{\top}UV^{\top}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}=\|\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}\|^{2}=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{(x_{k}^{(\psi)})^{2}}{n_{k}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi^{\top}((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}((\Phi\Phi^{\top})^{\dagger})^{1/2}\psi=(x^{(\psi)})^{\top}\bar{B}^{\top}VU^{\top}UV^{\top}\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}=\|\bar{B}x^{(\psi)}\|^{2}=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{(x_{k}^{(\psi)})^{2}}{n_{k}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Feature matching with alignment bias</h3>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In some applications we prefer <em id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">more reference-aligned</em> samples, even at the cost of reduced diversity.
We capture this tradeoff by scaling the target moment: for <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, define the loss with alignment bias as</p>
<table id="A3.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathcal{L}^{\alpha}_{\mathrm{FM}}(\theta)\!=\!\alpha\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\|\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|^{2}\big]\\
&amp;=\!\alpha\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{FM}}(\theta)\!-\!\underbrace{2(1-\alpha)\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]^{\top}\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big].}_{\text{alignment bias}}\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mphantom></mphantom></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>FM</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mpadded style="width:0.327em;" width="0.327em"><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.716em;" width="0.716em"><mo>=</mo></mpadded><mi>α</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.160em;" width="0.160em"><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mpadded style="width:0.716em;" width="0.716em"><mo>=</mo></mpadded><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>FM</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mpadded style="width:0.271em;" width="0.271em"><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mpadded></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.052em">−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>alignment bias</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathcal{L}^{\alpha}_{\mathrm{FM}}(\theta)\!=\!\alpha\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\|\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|^{2}\big]\\
&amp;=\!\alpha\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{FM}}(\theta)\!-\!\underbrace{2(1-\alpha)\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]^{\top}\!\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big].}_{\text{alignment bias}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The additional term explicitly encourages alignment between model and data features, making the objective <em id="A3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mode-seeking</em> as <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> decreases (typically improving accuracy and faithfulness but reducing diversity).
Operationally, this corresponds to multiplying the diversity terms in (<a href="#S2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Gradient estimation via REINFORCE. ‣ 2.2 Feature-matching rewards and on-policy training ‣ 2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Gradient estimation via REINFORCE. ‣ 2.2 Feature-matching rewards and on-policy training ‣ 2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) by <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, since the analogs of equations
(<a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 2.1 The feature-matching loss ‣ 2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)
and (<a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Gradient estimation via REINFORCE. ‣ 2.2 Feature-matching rewards and on-policy training ‣ 2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), (<a href="#S2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Gradient estimation via REINFORCE. ‣ 2.2 Feature-matching rewards and on-policy training ‣ 2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), and (<a href="#S2.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Gradient estimation via REINFORCE. ‣ 2.2 Feature-matching rewards and on-policy training ‣ 2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) are</p>
<table id="A3.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{L}^{\alpha}_{\mathrm{CFM}}(\theta)&amp;=\alpha\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\|\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\phi_{c}(y)\|^{2}\big],\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>CFM</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.160em;" width="0.160em"><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{L}^{\alpha}_{\mathrm{CFM}}(\theta)&amp;=\alpha\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\|\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\phi_{c}(y)\|^{2}\big],\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{L}^{\alpha}_{\mathrm{CFM}}(\theta;c,y)&amp;=\alpha\|\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\phi_{c}(y)\|^{2},\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>CFM</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.160em;" width="0.160em"><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{L}^{\alpha}_{\mathrm{CFM}}(\theta;c,y)&amp;=\alpha\|\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\phi_{c}(y)\|^{2},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}r(\hat{y},c)&amp;=2\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)-2\alpha\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\tilde{y})\big],\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}r(\hat{y},c)&amp;=2\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)-2\alpha\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\phi_{c}(\tilde{y})\big],\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}r_{j}&amp;=2\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)-\frac{2\alpha}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}}).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}r_{j}&amp;=2\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)-\frac{2\alpha}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}\neq j}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}}).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Note that when <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{\alpha}_{\mathrm{FM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>FM</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{\alpha}_{\mathrm{FM}}</annotation></semantics></math> is not a proper scoring rule, meaning that that it is not minimized by the ground truth distribution <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, and this can be seen in practice. In <a href="#A8.SS1" title="H.1 Sweeping across 𝛾, 𝛼 and warm-starting ‣ Appendix H Additional Experimental Results ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.1</span></a> we present experiments in which we sweep over <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> on all the tasks we consider: we consider the values <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\{0,0.5,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\{0,0.5,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We conclude that taking <math id="A3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> smaller helps in reducing the (unbiased) feature-matching loss faster, at the cost of a slower decrease of the CE loss, with stark differences in behavior depending on the value of <math id="A3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, when <math id="A3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, the CE loss decreases similarly fast for <math id="A3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\{0,0.5,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\{0,0.5,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, but when <math id="A3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0</annotation></semantics></math>, taking <math id="A3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\{0,0.5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\{0,0.5\}</annotation></semantics></math> causes the CE loss to diverge, while for <math id="A3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math> the CE loss still decreases monotonically, albeit at a slower rate than with higher <math id="A3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the CE term can help in stabilizing feature matching with alignment bias.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Feature matching with KL regularization</h3>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The feature matching loss with KL regularization with respect to a model <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> reads</p>
<table id="A4.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{FMKL}}(\theta)\!&amp;=\!\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\|\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|^{2}+{\textstyle\frac{1}{\beta}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\big(p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)\|\pi(\cdot|c)\big)\big]\\
&amp;=\!\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\|\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|^{2}+{\textstyle\frac{1}{\beta}}\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\log p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)-\log\pi(\hat{y}|c)\big]\big]\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>FMKL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.716em;" width="0.716em"><mo>=</mo></mpadded><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.160em;" width="0.160em"><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.716em;" width="0.716em"><mo>=</mo></mpadded><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mpadded style="width:0.160em;" width="0.160em"><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{FMKL}}(\theta)\!&amp;=\!\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\|\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|^{2}+{\textstyle\frac{1}{\beta}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\big(p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)\|\pi(\cdot|c)\big)\big]\\
&amp;=\!\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\big[\|\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(\hat{y})]\!-\!{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|^{2}+{\textstyle\frac{1}{\beta}}\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\big[\log p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)-\log\pi(\hat{y}|c)\big]\big]\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Observe that since this loss function decouples across different contexts <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following for all <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)=\arg\min_{\rho\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}\big\{{\textstyle\frac{1}{\beta}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\big(\rho\|\pi(\cdot|c)\big)+\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\rho}[\phi_{c}(y)]-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|_{2}^{2}\big\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>arg</mi><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>G</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)=\arg\min_{\rho\in\mathcal{V}^{G}}\big\{{\textstyle\frac{1}{\beta}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\big(\rho\|\pi(\cdot|c)\big)+\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\rho}[\phi_{c}(y)]-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|_{2}^{2}\big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Next, we will characterize the distribution <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes this loss function.
The following section contains some preliminary results.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Energy-based models with RKHS function classes</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following duality theorem relates two optimization problems which underlie energy-based models for which the energy class is a ball of the RKHS induced by a feature map <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Thm. 2, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Domingo-Enrich et al. (2022)</a></cite>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> be a base measure over a measurable space <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\beta}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\beta}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi:\mathcal{Y}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi:\mathcal{Y}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> be a feature map, and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consider the two problems</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\rho\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})}{\textstyle\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\rho\|\pi)+\|\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\rho}[\varphi(Y)]-v\|_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\rho\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})}{\textstyle\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\rho\|\pi)+\|\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\rho}[\varphi(Y)]-v\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}h\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\\
\|h\|_{2}\leq 1\end{subarray}}-v^{\top}h-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}}\log\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\pi}\big[\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\varphi(Y)^{\top}h\big)\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}h\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\\
\|h\|_{2}\leq 1\end{subarray}}-v^{\top}h-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}}\log\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\pi}\big[\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\varphi(Y)^{\top}h\big)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The problems (<a href="#A4.E70" title="Equation 70 ‣ Theorem D.1 (Thm. 2, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E71" title="Equation 71 ‣ Theorem D.1 (Thm. 2, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>) are convex.
The
problem (<a href="#A4.E71" title="Equation 71 ‣ Theorem D.1 (Thm. 2, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>) is the Fenchel dual of problem (<a href="#A4.E70" title="Equation 70 ‣ Theorem D.1 (Thm. 2, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>), and strong duality holds. Moreover, the solution
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> of (<a href="#A4.E70" title="Equation 70 ‣ Theorem D.1 (Thm. 2, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>) is unique and satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d\rho^{\star}}{d\pi}(y)=\frac{1}{Z_{\tilde{\beta}}}\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\varphi(y)^{\top}h^{\star}\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>Z</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d\rho^{\star}}{d\pi}(y)=\frac{1}{Z_{\tilde{\beta}}}\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\varphi(y)^{\top}h^{\star}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is a solution of (<a href="#A4.E71" title="Equation 71 ‣ Theorem D.1 (Thm. 2, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>) and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> is a normalization constant.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">And the following equivalence between minimization problems holds:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Prop. 3, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Domingo-Enrich et al. (2022)</a></cite>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the problem</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\rho\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})}\beta^{-1}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\rho\|\pi)+\|\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\rho}[\varphi(Y)]-v\|_{2}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\rho\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})}\beta^{-1}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\rho\|\pi)+\|\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\rho}[\varphi(Y)]-v\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Problems (<a href="#A4.E70" title="Equation 70 ‣ Theorem D.1 (Thm. 2, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E73" title="Equation 73 ‣ Theorem D.2 (Prop. 3, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) are equivalent in the following sense:
if <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{1}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{1}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is a solution of (<a href="#A4.E70" title="Equation 70 ‣ Theorem D.1 (Thm. 2, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>) for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, then it is also a solution of (<a href="#A4.E73" title="Equation 73 ‣ Theorem D.2 (Prop. 3, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) for</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta=\big(2\|\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\rho_{1}^{\star}}[\varphi(Y)]-v\|_{2}\big)^{-1}\tilde{\beta}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta=\big(2\|\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\rho_{1}^{\star}}[\varphi(Y)]-v\|_{2}\big)^{-1}\tilde{\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">provided that <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\rho_{1}^{\star}}[\varphi(Y)]-v\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\rho_{1}^{\star}}[\varphi(Y)]-v\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-zero. Conversely, if <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{2}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{2}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is a solution of (<a href="#A4.E73" title="Equation 73 ‣ Theorem D.2 (Prop. 3, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) for
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, then it is also a solution of (<a href="#A4.E70" title="Equation 70 ‣ Theorem D.1 (Thm. 2, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>) for</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\beta}=2\|\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\rho^{\star}_{2}}[\varphi(Y)]-v\|_{2}\beta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\beta}=2\|\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\rho^{\star}_{2}}[\varphi(Y)]-v\|_{2}\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model</h4>

<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the KL-regularized objective</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\min_{\rho}\;\;\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{\rho(\cdot\mid c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]-\mathbb{E}_{p(\cdot\mid c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big\|^{2}+\;{\textstyle\frac{1}{\beta}}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(\rho(\cdot|c)\,\|\,q(\cdot|c)\right)\Big],\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mphantom></mphantom></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.782em">+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mpadded style="width:0.686em;" width="0.686em"><mi>D</mi></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.062em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.507em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\min_{\rho}\;\;\mathbb{E}_{c\sim p}\Big[\big\|\mathbb{E}_{\rho(\cdot\mid c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]-\mathbb{E}_{p(\cdot\mid c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big\|^{2}+\;{\textstyle\frac{1}{\beta}}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(\rho(\cdot|c)\,\|\,q(\cdot|c)\right)\Big],\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> controls the strength of the regularization. the solution to (<a href="#A4.E76" title="Equation 76 ‣ Theorem D.3. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">76</span></a>) has the form of an exponential tilt of the base distribution,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho^{\star}(y|c)\propto q(y|c)\,\exp\!\big(-\chi_{c}^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>χ</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho^{\star}(y|c)\propto q(y|c)\,\exp\!\big(-\chi_{c}^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for a context-dependent vector <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{c}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{c}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> chosen to optimize:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E77.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\|\chi\|_{2}\leq\tilde{\beta}}\big\{-\big({\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}-1\big)\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}\chi+\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}\big[\log\rho_{\chi}(y|c)\big]\big\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>χ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\|\chi\|_{2}\leq\tilde{\beta}}\big\{-\big({\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}-1\big)\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}\chi+\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}\big[\log\rho_{\chi}(y|c)\big]\big\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\chi}(y|c)\propto q(y|c)\,\exp\!\big(-\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>χ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\chi}(y|c)\propto q(y|c)\,\exp\!\big(-\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\big)</annotation></semantics></math>,
for a <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\beta}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\beta}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that depends on <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. Two values of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> admit specific interpretations:</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For pure EBFT (</span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">), the optimal </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>χ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the </span><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">maximum likelihood estimate</span><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">: When </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the problem (</span><a href="#A4.E77" title="Equation 77 ‣ Theorem D.3. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">77</span></a><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) simplifies to:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\|\chi\|_{2}\leq\tilde{\beta}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}\big[\log\rho_{\chi}(y|c)\big]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>χ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\|\chi\|_{2}\leq\tilde{\beta}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}\big[\log\rho_{\chi}(y|c)\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This corresponds to the maximum likelihood loss function for an energy-based model with
energy function
</span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(y,c)=\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(y,c)=\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(y).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{+}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{+}=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the optimal </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>χ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> has the </span><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">same direction as the ground-truth mean feature</span><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">: When </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the problem (</span><a href="#A4.E77" title="Equation 77 ‣ Theorem D.3. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">77</span></a><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) is equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E79.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\chi\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\\
\|\chi\|_{2}\leq\tilde{\beta}\end{subarray}}-\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}\chi," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\chi\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\\
\|\chi\|_{2}\leq\tilde{\beta}\end{subarray}}-\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}\chi,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which has optimal solution</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\chi^{\star}=-\tilde{\beta}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]}{\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big\|_{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\chi^{\star}=-\tilde{\beta}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]}{\big\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\big\|_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus, for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the solution <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> of (<a href="#A4.E77" title="Equation 77 ‣ Theorem D.3. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">77</span></a>) interpolates between the maximum likelihood estimate and the rescaled ground-truth mean feature.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given a context <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, and a completion length <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, let us apply <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1 (Thm. 2, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> and <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem D.2 (Prop. 3, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> by setting <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}=\mathcal{V}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>G</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}=\mathcal{V}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(y)=\phi_{c}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(y)=\phi_{c}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi=\pi(\cdot|c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\pi(\cdot|c)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v={\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v={\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, the problems (<a href="#A4.E70" title="Equation 70 ‣ Theorem D.1 (Thm. 2, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>), (<a href="#A4.E73" title="Equation 73 ‣ Theorem D.2 (Prop. 3, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E71" title="Equation 71 ‣ Theorem D.1 (Thm. 2, ( ) ). ‣ D.1 Energy-based models with RKHS function classes ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>) take the form</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E81.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\rho\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})}{\textstyle\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\big(\rho\|\pi(\cdot|c)\big)+\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\rho}[\phi_{c}(y)]-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\rho\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})}{\textstyle\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\big(\rho\|\pi(\cdot|c)\big)+\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\rho}[\phi_{c}(y)]-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E82.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\rho\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})}{\textstyle\frac{1}{\beta}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\big(\rho\|\pi(\cdot|c)\big)+\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\rho}[\phi_{c}(y)]-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|_{2}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\rho\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})}{\textstyle\frac{1}{\beta}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\big(\rho\|\pi(\cdot|c)\big)+\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\rho}[\phi_{c}(y)]-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E83.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}h\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\\
\|h\|_{2}\leq 1\end{subarray}}-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}h-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}}\log\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|c)}\big[\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\phi_{c}(y)^{\top}h\big)\big]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}h\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\\
\|h\|_{2}\leq 1\end{subarray}}-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}h-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}}\log\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|c)}\big[\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\phi_{c}(y)^{\top}h\big)\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Problem (<a href="#A4.E82" title="Equation 82 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">82</span></a>) is the KL-regularized feature-matching objective with alignment bias,
if we absorb the constant <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> accompanying <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\rho}[\phi_{c}(y)]-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\rho}[\phi_{c}(y)]-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> into the constants <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.
The (unique) solution (<a href="#A4.E81" title="Equation 81 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">81</span></a>) of <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and the solution <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> of (<a href="#A4.E83" title="Equation 83 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">83</span></a>) are related by the equation</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho^{\star}(y)=\frac{\pi(y|c)\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\phi_{c}(y)^{\top}h^{\star}\big)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}}\pi(y^{\prime}|c)\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\phi_{c}(y^{\prime})^{\top}h^{\star}\big)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho^{\star}(y)=\frac{\pi(y|c)\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\phi_{c}(y)^{\top}h^{\star}\big)}{\sum_{y^{\prime}}\pi(y^{\prime}|c)\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\phi_{c}(y^{\prime})^{\top}h^{\star}\big)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is also the (unique) solution of (<a href="#A4.E82" title="Equation 82 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">82</span></a>) provided that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E85.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\beta}=2\|\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\rho^{\star}}[\varphi(Y)]-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|_{2}\beta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\beta}=2\|\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim\rho^{\star}}[\varphi(Y)]-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]\|_{2}\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that the problem (<a href="#A4.E82" title="Equation 82 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">82</span></a>) is equal to the problem (<a href="#A4.E69" title="Equation 69 ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>), which means that (<a href="#A4.E81" title="Equation 81 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">81</span></a>)-(<a href="#A4.E83" title="Equation 83 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">83</span></a>) characterize the optimal <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen according to (<a href="#A4.E85" title="Equation 85 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">85</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we focus on the problem (<a href="#A4.E83" title="Equation 83 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">83</span></a>). We define <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\tilde{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\tilde{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the following class of energy functions:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{E}_{\tilde{\beta}}&amp;=\{E:\mathcal{V}^{G}\to\mathbb{R}\,|\,\exists\chi\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\mathrm{s.t.}\|\chi\|_{2}\leq\tilde{\beta},\mathrm{and}\,\forall x\in\mathcal{V}^{G},\,E(x)=\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(x)\}\\
&amp;=\{E:\mathcal{V}^{G}\to\mathbb{R}\,|\,\exists h\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\mathrm{s.t.}\|h\|_{2}\leq 1,\mathrm{and}\,\forall x\in\mathcal{V}^{G},\,E(x)=\tilde{\beta}h^{\top}\phi_{c}(x)\},\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.340em" rspace="0.507em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>and</mi><mo lspace="0.507em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.507em">,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.340em" rspace="0.507em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>and</mi><mo lspace="0.507em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.507em">,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{E}_{\tilde{\beta}}&amp;=\{E:\mathcal{V}^{G}\to\mathbb{R}\,|\,\exists\chi\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\mathrm{s.t.}\|\chi\|_{2}\leq\tilde{\beta},\mathrm{and}\,\forall x\in\mathcal{V}^{G},\,E(x)=\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(x)\}\\
&amp;=\{E:\mathcal{V}^{G}\to\mathbb{R}\,|\,\exists h\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\mathrm{s.t.}\|h\|_{2}\leq 1,\mathrm{and}\,\forall x\in\mathcal{V}^{G},\,E(x)=\tilde{\beta}h^{\top}\phi_{c}(x)\},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">and given <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\chi},\rho^{(\tilde{\beta})}_{h}\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{V}^{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>χ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>G</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\chi},\rho^{(\tilde{\beta})}_{h}\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{V}^{G})</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho_{\chi}(y)=\frac{\pi(y|c)\exp\big(-\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\big)}{\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi(\cdot|c)}\big[\exp\big(-\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(y^{\prime})\big)\big]},\qquad\rho^{(\tilde{\beta})}_{h}(y)=\frac{\pi(y|c)\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\big)}{\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi(\cdot|c)}\big[\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(y^{\prime})\big)\big]}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>χ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>χ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho_{\chi}(y)=\frac{\pi(y|c)\exp\big(-\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\big)}{\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi(\cdot|c)}\big[\exp\big(-\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(y^{\prime})\big)\big]},\qquad\rho^{(\tilde{\beta})}_{h}(y)=\frac{\pi(y|c)\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\big)}{\mathbb{E}_{y^{\prime}\sim\pi(\cdot|c)}\big[\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\chi^{\top}\phi_{c}(y^{\prime})\big)\big]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">We rewrite the problem (<a href="#A4.E83" title="Equation 83 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">83</span></a>) as</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}h\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\\
\|h\|_{2}\leq 1\end{subarray}}-\big({\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}-1\big)\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}h-\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}h-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}}\log\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|c)}\big[\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\phi_{c}(y)^{\top}h\big)\big]\\
&amp;=\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}h\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\\
\|h\|_{2}\leq 1\end{subarray}}-\big({\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}-1\big)\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}h+\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}\Big[\log\frac{\rho^{(\tilde{\beta})}_{h}(y)}{\pi(y|c)}\Big]\\
&amp;=\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}h\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\\
\|h\|_{2}\leq 1\end{subarray}}-\big({\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}-1\big)\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}h+\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}\Big[\log\rho^{(\tilde{\beta})}_{h}(y)\Big]+\mathrm{const}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mphantom></mphantom></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>const</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}h\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\\
\|h\|_{2}\leq 1\end{subarray}}-\big({\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}-1\big)\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}h-\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}h-{\textstyle\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}}\log\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|c)}\big[\exp\big(-\tilde{\beta}\phi_{c}(y)^{\top}h\big)\big]\\
&amp;=\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}h\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\\
\|h\|_{2}\leq 1\end{subarray}}-\big({\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}-1\big)\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}h+\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}\Big[\log\frac{\rho^{(\tilde{\beta})}_{h}(y)}{\pi(y|c)}\Big]\\
&amp;=\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}h\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\\
\|h\|_{2}\leq 1\end{subarray}}-\big({\textstyle\frac{1}{\alpha}}-1\big)\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}[\phi_{c}(y)]^{\top}h+\frac{1}{\tilde{\beta}}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p(\cdot|c)}\Big[\log\rho^{(\tilde{\beta})}_{h}(y)\Big]+\mathrm{const}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Writing the right-hand side problem in terms of <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>χ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, and multiplying the objective by <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, yields the problem in (<a href="#A4.E77" title="Equation 77 ‣ Theorem D.3. ‣ D.2 Feature matching with KL regularization as an implicit energy-based model ‣ Appendix D Feature matching with KL regularization ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">77</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Computing the REINFORCE gradient and the RLOO baseline for EBFT</h3>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We derive the REINFORCE gradient first. Rewriting <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{L}}_{\mathrm{FM}}(\theta;c,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>FM</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{L}}_{\mathrm{FM}}(\theta;c,y)</annotation></semantics></math> explicitly in terms of <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and using that <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{y}</annotation></semantics></math> play a symmetric role, we have the following:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\tilde{\mathcal{L}}_{\mathrm{FM}}(\theta;c,y)\\
&amp;=\!\nabla_{\theta}\Big(\sum_{\hat{y},\tilde{y}}p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)p_{\theta}(\tilde{y}|c)\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\phi_{c}(\tilde{y})-2\sum_{\hat{y}}p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\Big)\\
&amp;=\!\sum_{\hat{y},\tilde{y}}\Big(\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)+\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\tilde{y}|c)\Big)p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)p_{\theta}(\tilde{y}|c)\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\phi_{c}(\tilde{y})-2\sum_{\hat{y}}\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\\
&amp;=\!2\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y},\tilde{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\!\Big[\nabla\log p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\!\phi_{c}(\tilde{y})\Big]-2\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\Big[\nabla\log p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\Big].\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>FM</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mpadded style="width:0.716em;" width="0.716em"><mo>=</mo></mpadded><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mpadded><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\tilde{\mathcal{L}}_{\mathrm{FM}}(\theta;c,y)\\
&amp;=\!\nabla_{\theta}\Big(\sum_{\hat{y},\tilde{y}}p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)p_{\theta}(\tilde{y}|c)\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\phi_{c}(\tilde{y})-2\sum_{\hat{y}}p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\Big)\\
&amp;=\!\sum_{\hat{y},\tilde{y}}\Big(\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)+\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\tilde{y}|c)\Big)p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)p_{\theta}(\tilde{y}|c)\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\phi_{c}(\tilde{y})-2\sum_{\hat{y}}\nabla_{\theta}\log p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\\
&amp;=\!2\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y},\tilde{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\!\Big[\nabla\log p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\!\phi_{c}(\tilde{y})\Big]-2\mathbb{E}_{\hat{y}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot|c)}\Big[\nabla\log p_{\theta}(\hat{y}|c)\phi_{c}(\hat{y})^{\top}\phi_{c}(y)\Big].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Next, we derive the RLOO baseline. Define</p>
<table id="A5.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{1}^{(j)}=2\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\phi_{c}(y),\qquad T_{2}^{(j)}=\frac{2}{n\!-\!1}\!\!\sum_{j^{\prime}=1,j^{\prime}\neq j}^{n}\!\!\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{1}^{(j)}=2\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\phi_{c}(y),\qquad T_{2}^{(j)}=\frac{2}{n\!-\!1}\!\!\sum_{j^{\prime}=1,j^{\prime}\neq j}^{n}\!\!\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which means that we can rewrite the REINFORCE gradient (<a href="#S2.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Gradient estimation via REINFORCE. ‣ 2.2 Feature-matching rewards and on-policy training ‣ 2 Language Modeling with Feature Matching ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>)</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">as</p>
<table id="A5.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E91.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\nabla\log p_{\theta}(Y^{(j)}|c)\big(T_{1}^{(j)}-T_{2}^{(j)}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\nabla\log p_{\theta}(Y^{(j)}|c)\big(T_{1}^{(j)}-T_{2}^{(j)}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We want to use a baseline <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> to reduce the variance of the gradient estimate (<a href="#A5.E91" title="Equation 91 ‣ Appendix E Computing the REINFORCE gradient and the RLOO baseline for EBFT ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">91</span></a>). That is, the estimate with baseline <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> reads</p>
<table id="A5.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E92.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\nabla\log p_{\theta}(Y^{(j)}|c)\big(T_{1}^{(j)}-T_{2}^{(j)}-b^{(j)}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\nabla\log p_{\theta}(Y^{(j)}|c)\big(T_{1}^{(j)}-T_{2}^{(j)}-b^{(j)}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">For the baselined gradient estimate to be unbiased, we need that <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A naive RLOO baseline would be <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{(j)}=\frac{1}{N-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}=1,j^{\prime}\neq j}^{N}\big(T_{1}^{(j^{\prime})}-T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{(j)}=\frac{1}{N-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}=1,j^{\prime}\neq j}^{N}\big(T_{1}^{(j^{\prime})}-T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. simply averaging the rewards for all rollouts except the <math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th one. However, the terms <math id="A5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math> are not independent of <math id="A5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which means that this baseline is not independent of <math id="A5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>. To obtain an independent baseline, we need to replace <math id="A5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}^{(j^{\prime},j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}^{(j^{\prime},j)}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as</p>
<table id="A5.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}T_{2}^{(j^{\prime},j)}&amp;=\frac{2}{n-2}\sum_{j^{\prime\prime}=1,\,j^{\prime\prime}\neq j^{\prime},j}^{n}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime\prime}})^{\top}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})=\frac{2}{n-2}\Big(\sum_{j^{\prime\prime}=1,j^{\prime\prime}\neq j^{\prime}}^{n}\varphi(c\!:\!\hat{y}_{j^{\prime\prime}})^{\top}\varphi(c\!:\!\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})-\varphi(c\!:\!\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\varphi(c\!:\!\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})\Big)\\
&amp;=\frac{n-1}{n-2}T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}-\frac{2}{n-2}\varphi(c\!:\!\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\varphi(c\!:\!\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}}).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mo rspace="0.108em">:</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mo rspace="0.108em">:</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mo rspace="0.108em">:</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mo rspace="0.108em">:</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mo rspace="0.108em">:</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.371em;" width="0.371em"><mi>c</mi></mpadded><mo rspace="0.108em">:</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}T_{2}^{(j^{\prime},j)}&amp;=\frac{2}{n-2}\sum_{j^{\prime\prime}=1,\,j^{\prime\prime}\neq j^{\prime},j}^{n}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime\prime}})^{\top}\phi_{c}(\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})=\frac{2}{n-2}\Big(\sum_{j^{\prime\prime}=1,j^{\prime\prime}\neq j^{\prime}}^{n}\varphi(c\!:\!\hat{y}_{j^{\prime\prime}})^{\top}\varphi(c\!:\!\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})-\varphi(c\!:\!\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\varphi(c\!:\!\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}})\Big)\\
&amp;=\frac{n-1}{n-2}T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}-\frac{2}{n-2}\varphi(c\!:\!\hat{y}_{j})^{\top}\varphi(c\!:\!\hat{y}_{j^{\prime}}).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the baseline that we end up with is:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}b^{(j)}&amp;=\frac{1}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}=1,j^{\prime}\neq j}^{n}\big(T_{1}^{(j^{\prime})}-T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}\big)\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}=1,j^{\prime}\neq j}^{n}\Big(T_{1}^{(j^{\prime})}-\Big(\frac{n-1}{n-2}T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}-\frac{2}{n-2}\phi(Y^{(j)})^{\top}\phi(Y^{(j^{\prime})})\Big)\Big)\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}=1,j^{\prime}\neq j}^{n}T_{1}^{(j^{\prime})}-\frac{1}{n-2}\sum_{j^{\prime}=1,j^{\prime}\neq j}^{n}T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}+\frac{1}{n-2}T_{2}^{(j)}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}b^{(j)}&amp;=\frac{1}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}=1,j^{\prime}\neq j}^{n}\big(T_{1}^{(j^{\prime})}-T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}\big)\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}=1,j^{\prime}\neq j}^{n}\Big(T_{1}^{(j^{\prime})}-\Big(\frac{n-1}{n-2}T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}-\frac{2}{n-2}\phi(Y^{(j)})^{\top}\phi(Y^{(j^{\prime})})\Big)\Big)\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{n-1}\sum_{j^{\prime}=1,j^{\prime}\neq j}^{n}T_{1}^{(j^{\prime})}-\frac{1}{n-2}\sum_{j^{\prime}=1,j^{\prime}\neq j}^{n}T_{2}^{(j^{\prime})}+\frac{1}{n-2}T_{2}^{(j)}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Details on the strided parallel rollout procedure</h3>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sampling from a single, unstructured sequence provides only one supervision point and is a major bottleneck for EBFT, particularly because each sample must be embedded via forward passes through a separate feature network. Instead, we treat a single training sequence as a source of multiple nested prompts by identifying many anchor points along the text. Sampling from these points sequentially is prohibitively expensive, so we implement a novel parallel generation pipeline that simultaneously samples from different anchor points in one forward pass, similar to the custom attention mask approach introduced by Quiet-STaR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zelikman et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
Given a starting sequence <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{0:T-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0:T-1}</annotation></semantics></math> of length <math id="A6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, a stride <math id="A6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, and a generation length <math id="A6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, we construct a set of nested prompts by segmenting <math id="A6.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{0:T-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0:T-1}</annotation></semantics></math> every <math id="A6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> tokens. This yields <math id="A6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\lfloor\frac{T-G}{s}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\lfloor\frac{T-G}{s}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> nested prompts. For each prompt <math id="A6.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c_{b}=x_{0:bs}\quad(b=1,\ldots,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{b}=x_{0:bs}\quad(b=1,\ldots,B)</annotation></semantics></math>, we take the next <math id="A6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens in the original sequence <math id="A6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> as the ground-truth continuation <math id="A6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding <math id="A6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(c_{b},y_{b})\}_{b=1}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(c_{b},y_{b})\}_{b=1}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math> ground truth context and completion pairs. Additionally, from each prompt, we sample a continuation <math id="A6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> of length <math id="A6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. Using our custom mask, we can sample one token from each prefix in just one forward pass. We can then obtain <math id="A6.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{y}_{b}\}_{b=1}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{y}_{b}\}_{b=1}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math> length <math id="A6.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> model completions in <math id="A6.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> forward passes.
The resulting <math id="A6.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BG" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BG</annotation></semantics></math> generated tokens are appended in generation order; for example, with <math id="A6.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=2</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\hat{y}_{1,0},\hat{y}_{2,0},\hat{y}_{3,0},\;\hat{y}_{1,1},\hat{y}_{2,1},\hat{y}_{3,1}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\hat{y}_{1,0},\hat{y}_{2,0},\hat{y}_{3,0},\;\hat{y}_{1,1},\hat{y}_{2,1},\hat{y}_{3,1}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This interleaving supports an efficient reshape into per-block windows for downstream scoring and feature extraction.
In particular, we exploit the same strided structure to compute features for all generated blocks (and their ground-truth counterparts) with a single batched call to the feature network, followed by a reshape/indexing step to recover per-block embeddings.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A6.F9" title="In Appendix F Details on the strided parallel rollout procedure ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> shows a sketch of the strided parallel rollout procedure for a sequence of length <math id="A6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=12</annotation></semantics></math>, stride <math id="A6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=4</annotation></semantics></math> and completion length <math id="A6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=4</annotation></semantics></math>, which means that <math id="A6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\lfloor(12-4)/4\rfloor=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\lfloor(12-4)/4\rfloor=2</annotation></semantics></math> context-completion pairs are used: <math id="A6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}=(t_{i})_{i=0}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}=(t_{i})_{i=0}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}=(t_{i})_{i=4}^{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}=(t_{i})_{i=4}^{7}</annotation></semantics></math>; and <math id="A6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=(t_{i})_{i=0}^{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=(t_{i})_{i=0}^{7}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{2}=(t_{i})_{i=8}^{11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mn>11</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{2}=(t_{i})_{i=8}^{11}</annotation></semantics></math>. The ground truth sequence is in blue, and the generated completions are in red and green: <math id="A6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{1}=(t_{i\,a})_{i=4}^{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{1}=(t_{i\,a})_{i=4}^{7}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{2}=(t_{i\,b})_{i=8}^{11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mn>11</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{2}=(t_{i\,b})_{i=8}^{11}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.12248v1/images/branching_generation_paths_big_font.png" id="A6.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/189;" width="381" height="189" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A6.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Strided parallel rollouts for a sequence of length <math id="A6.F9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=12</annotation></semantics></math>, stride <math id="A6.F9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=4</annotation></semantics></math> and completion length <math id="A6.F9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm to obtain the generated completions <math id="A6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> involves four model calls to <math id="A6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. <a href="#A6.F9" title="In Appendix F Details on the strided parallel rollout procedure ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> shows a sketch of the generated tokens using the strided parallel rollout procedure, and <a href="#A6.EGx90" title="In Appendix F Details on the strided parallel rollout procedure ‣ Matching Features, Not Tokens: Energy-Based Fine-Tuning of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> shows the custom attention matrix for the fourth call (the horizontal and vertical lines show the three top left custom matrices used for the first three calls).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F10" class="ltx_figure">
<table id="A6.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.EGx90.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.EGx90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\left[\begin{array}[]{cccccccc|cc|cc|cc}0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty\\
0&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty\\
\hline\cr 0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty\\
\hline\cr 0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty\\
\hline\cr 0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;\infty&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;0&amp;\infty&amp;0&amp;\infty\\
