<span id="A8.F15.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A8.F15.pic1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="102.89" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 434.07 102.89" width="434.07"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,102.89) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E11D48;" fill="#E11D48" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 2.21 L 0 100.67 C 0 101.89 0.99 102.89 2.21 102.89 L 431.86 102.89 C 433.08 102.89 434.07 101.89 434.07 100.67 L 434.07 2.21 C 434.07 0.99 433.08 0 431.86 0 L 2.21 0 C 0.99 0 0 0.99 0 2.21 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF1F2;" fill="#FFF1F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.55 2.21 L 0.55 100.67 C 0.55 101.59 1.3 102.33 2.21 102.33 L 431.86 102.33 C 432.77 102.33 433.52 101.59 433.52 100.67 L 433.52 2.21 C 433.52 1.3 432.77 0.55 431.86 0.55 L 2.21 0.55 C 1.3 0.55 0.55 1.3 0.55 2.21 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 7.47 90.49)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.29em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:6.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="93.48" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="419.13"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A8.F15.pic1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.29em;">
<span id="A8.F15.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.F15.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#E11D48;">Failure mode:</span><span id="A8.F15.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> Base uses non-overlapping <span id="A8.F15.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">count</span>; SFT/RLVR advance by <span id="A8.F15.pic1.p2.pic1.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">len(substring)</span> (non-overlapping), missing overlaps.
</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A8.F15.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 15</span>: </span><span id="A8.F15.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">HumanEval/18: counting overlapping substring occurrences.<span id="A8.F15.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> EBFT correctly advances by one character after each match and therefore counts overlapping occurrences. By contrast, the base model uses Python’s non-overlapping <span id="A8.F15.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">string.count</span>, while both SFT and RLVR advance by <span id="A8.F15.7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">len(substring)</span>, which misses overlap-sensitive cases and causes test failures.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
