<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A8.F16.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 16</span>: </span><span id="A8.F16.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">HumanEval/94: largest prime digit sum.<span id="A8.F16.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> EBFT produces a self-contained executable solution by defining <span id="A8.F16.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">is_prime</span> and then computing the digit sum of the largest prime in the list. The base model and RLVR instead rely on an undefined helper function, while SFT truncates mid-function and yields syntactically invalid Python, illustrating a recurring executability gap between EBFT and the competing methods.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
